  "goodToKnow": "Die Anlehnung appears mostly in the phrase in Anlehnung an (based on, modelled on, in reference to): ein Design in Anlehnung an die 70er-Jahre, ein Titel in Anlehnung an Goethe. It's common in formal writing, art criticism and academic texts. The verb anlehnen means to lean: das Fahrrad an die Wand lehnen, and sich anlehnen means to lean on someone, also emotionally. The door can be angelehnt (left ajar)."
